DESCRIPTION:Do you want to know how to sew your own clothes? Do you know a
 bsolutely nothing about sewing clothes? Barbie and I can help!\nThere's a 
 lot more that goes into making clothes than poking a string through some c
 loth. This is a workshop for people who want to sew but have no idea how t
 o get started. Everyone who attends will design a piece of clothing\, make
  the pattern\, prepare the fabric\, cut the pieces\, and hand-stitch it to
 gether in a 3-hour period. The catch is that it won't be for you\, it'll b
 e for Barbie.\nDon't worry though! Once you've seen the process through an
 d learned each step\, the skills can be scaled up to whatever dimensions y
 our real body has. Barbie is a convenient model because she's just shy of 
 twelve inches tall\, but the process is exactly the same for humans too.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T192019Z
LOCATION:HackLab.TO\n1677 St Clair Ave W\, Toronto ON M6N 1H9\, Canada
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
