SUMMARY:Toronto Contra Dance with David Smukler and Kaw Creek
DESCRIPTION:Make your Saturday night count – join us on the Danforth for live tunes\, lively dancing\, and a room full of good energy.\n✨ On stage:\nCaller David Smukler guiding the dances\, with Kaw Creek setting the pulse and keeping the floor in motion all night long.\n🕖 Evening timeline:\n7:00 PM – Beginner lesson (no partner or experience needed)\n7:30 PM – Dancing gets underway\n😷 Mask-Optional\n💧 Bring a refillable water bottle\n🥟 Samosas will be ready (arrive early if you want one!)\nSliding scale: $7–$35 (kids 16 & under free)\nIt costs about $22 per dancer to make these nights happen—your support\, generosity\, and word-of-mouth keep the community strong.\n📍 St. Barnabas Church Hall\n175 Hampton Ave (near Chester Station)\n🌐 https://www.tcdance.org/\nWhether it’s your first dance or your fiftieth\, we’d love to see you there. ❤️
