SUMMARY:Introductory Piano: Adult Learning Circles in 4 Sessions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T160000
UID:6aba74d1101eb7003f338379@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to learn how to play the piano?\nIf you a
 re 18 years or older\, no age limit\, join us for four adult learning circ
 les led by a professional pianist. You will learn the basic piano includin
 g note recognition\, finger placing\, and simple songs. There will be oppo
 rtunities for one-on-one instruction for each participant on a baby grand 
 piano.\nFor absolute beginners only. One-time registration for all four se
 ssions starts on Monday\, October 5\, 2026 at 10am on tpl.ca. Since each s
 ession builds on the last and space is limited\, we ask that you only regi
 ster if you can attend all four weeks.\nPlease do not register if you have
  previously participated at the piano circles at the Toronto Public Librar
 y.\nNo drop-ins\, by registration only.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aba74d1101eb7003f338379
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
