SUMMARY:The Sunday Night with Friends Dinner Party 
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nGood day everyone\,\
 n\nJoin us for **The Sunday Night with Friends Dinner Party**. A warm and 
 welcoming evening created for meeting new people\, enjoying good conversat
 ion and sharing a relaxed meal together.\n\n\\*Joined by my other social g
 roups too\; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn out with lots of friendly
  peers\n\n\\*Please note we are at **The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 
 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Lawrence - south of the 401 **(we w
 ill be in the back dining area)**\n\n*\\*You can ask the bartender if you 
 like to show you to the group (simply ask for Steve's dinner party)*\n\n-Y
 ou'll find it's a cozy\, relaxed and enjoyable atmosphere!\n\n**-Free Park
 ing found on residential side streets**\n\n(Event Details Below)\n\nSincer
 ely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\nEvent Details:\n**The Sunday 
 Night with Friends Dinner Party**\n\nLooking for a fun and relaxed way to 
 enjoy your Sunday evening?\n\n\\* 🍽️ Enjoy a delicious dinner in a re
 laxed\, friendly setting.\n\\* 😊 Meet new people and reconnect with fam
 iliar faces.\n\\* 💬 Great conversation\, laughter\, and a welcoming soc
 ial atmosphere.\n\n**Dinner Party Topics: (Optional)** may include but not
  limited too: Travel\, Culture\, Spirituality\, Relationships\, Modern Dat
 ing\, Work/Life balance\, Life after Marriage\, Dating Apps\, Comedy\, His
 tory\, Art\, Technology\, Economy\, Music\, Movies\, Sports\, Fashion\, Ho
 bbies\, Books\, Psychology\, Philosophy\, the Future\, History\, Pop Cultu
 re\, Theatre\, etc.)\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:** 5 dollars (Cash on
 ly at the door) (HST included)\nor by e transfer: **steveflemming11@gmail.
 com**\n\n***\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\n-Arrive any time between 6:00 p
 m and 7:00 pm (if you can) (please ask for Steve when you arrive-\n\\*Grea
 t dinner menu and food specials provided:\n(One beverage or appetizer mini
 mum upon arrival to support venue)\n\n**Parking and Transportation:**\n\\*
 Lots of street parking on avenue and free residential parking\nhttps://www
 .firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/\n\n(15-20 minute walk from Yonge & L
 awrence subway station-or simply take bus or uber from the station)
