X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:The InSECT Program\, on Science Education\, Citizenship\, and Trut
 h
DTSTART:20261027T140000Z
DTEND:20261027T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20261019T202500Z
UID:MEC-4135e6160b631ba9d74c58e11136d6f8@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261027T140000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Science,FSc Science, Technology &amp\; Society
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261019
DESCRIPTION:Harry Collins (Cardiff / UCL Institute of Education)\nA propos
 ed new interdisciplinary teaching program in which science and engineering
  students learn alongside arts and humanities students\, so that science t
 eaching also becomes an education in democratic knowledge making instead o
 f a purely technical exercise. Over the past half-century\, historians\, s
 ociologists and philosophers have shown how scientific truth is constructe
 d. From this many have concluded that science should be levelled down and 
 brought into line with social values. We argue the opposite: science is an
  institution committed to correspondence truth about the observable world 
 and to the moral duty of scientists to report their findings honestly. Thi
 s makes science a model for democratic decision making and a bulwark again
 st populists and autocrats\, who are trying to erode truth in order to red
 efine ‘the will of the people’ however they please.\nThis is a virtual
  event as our speaker is joining us from the UK\; please register in advan
 ce by emailing stsadmin@yorku.ca ( mailto:stsadmin@yorku.ca ) to receive m
 eeting link.\n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261021
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-insect-program-on-science-education
 -citizenship-and-truth/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
