BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_4h7dspldpuviiv4o1slj9o5p5c
X-SOURCE:CITA Seminars
DTSTART:20261027T150000Z
DTEND:20261027T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T043526Z
UID:oicmhgj89d95ci57inp4fl7r3c@google.com
CREATED:20261022T150828Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Title: <b>Black Holes-- Entropy container or creator</b></p>
 \n\n<p>Abstract: The usual model of a black hole is that after it has been 
 created it contains entropy proportional to M^2\, (or 1/4 the surface area 
 of the horizon). It is like the cooling off of a hot lump of coal or the em
 ission of radiation by a hot black body radiator. I will argue that a bette
 r analogy is an amplifier (like in your radio) for which there is a constan
 t flux of radiation which is created by the amplification process\, but whi
 ch does not have a large internal\nentropy which slowly leaks out. I will i
 llustrate this by a simple\, exactly solvable model of an amplifier and of 
 a 2-D black hole.</p>\n<p>Host: <b>Anupam Mazumdar</b></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261022T151005Z
LOCATION:MP 1318A
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bill Unruh (UBC)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
