URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/24077/1793116800000
SUMMARY: Cylinder Spectrum & Polygon Plexus
DESCRIPTION:"Cylinder Spectrum" & "Polygon Plexus" are two visual art exh
 ibitions by Toronto artist Angela Julian (Native Torontonian and OCADU gr
 aduate). Both shows are located inside the Sun Gallery at 918 Bathurst Ar
 ts & Culture Center. The collected works are a group of large scale color
 ful abstract paintings done in plaster. They range in size\, scale\, shap
 e\, and number\, but they are all tied together through the mediums of pl
 aster and acrylic paint.\n\n\nOn one side of the gallery is the show "Cyl
 inder Spectrum"\, which is a group of acrylic paintings done on distinctl
 y rounded canvases that were covered in layers of mixed-media and plaster
 . These are shown both as individual works and presented as a group that 
 makeup a larger installation. The circular nature of the canvases and sur
 faces links the entire show by their rounded nature. On the opposite side
  of the gallery is the show "Polygon Plexus" which is a group of hand-mad
 e canvases and surfaces that were created to form irregular shapes. These
  outer shapes are deliberately jagged\, pointed\, elongated\, and heavily
  textured surfaces\, and each painting is covered with a either a geometr
 ic or abstract pattern. Both exhibitions demonstrate a variety of differe
 nt color schemes and embrace vibrant\, highly-saturated colors.\n\n\nThe 
 Sun Gallery is the twin space to the Star Gallery on the property\, and i
 t is an airy and brilliantly lit space with wide sky-lights that allow fo
 r beautiful natural day-light. The gallery space is located at 918 Bathur
 st Arts & Culture Center in the Annex neighborhood (Bloor / Bathurst area
 ). The center is a historic building in Toronto and was formerly a Buddhi
 st Temple before it became a venue for Arts and Culture. It has an in-hou
 se audience that ranges from both broad to local. With many disappearing 
 gallery spaces in Toronto\, it proudly boasts its survival and longevity 
 as a space within the landscape of an ever-changing metropolis city. The 
 interior of 918 Bathurst is a mix of modern design elements in conjunctio
 n with its preserved historic architecture\, notably the beautiful wooden
  beams of its ceilings. These are two very fun shows and run until the en
 d of October\, 2026.\n\nUpcoming Events | 918 Bathurst Centre for Culture
 \, Arts\, Media and Education https://www.918bathurst.com/events
CATEGORIES:Art-Show/Gallery-Event,918-Bathurst-Arts-and-Culture-Center
