BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/climate-talks-water-canada-germany-road-to-the-un-water-conference/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Climate Talks Water\, Canada-Germany: Road to the UN Water Confere
 nce
DTSTART:20261027T170000Z
DTEND:20261027T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T202800Z
UID:MEC-6a6a73c9c5eecb746b0ab4c888939818@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261027T170000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 10/50518a55-0d0b-4aa5-b74a-985f5ec04aab-1-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Science,International,Lassonde School of Engineering
 ,Research &amp\; Innovation
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261023
DESCRIPTION:\nYork University\, in collaboration with the Embassy and Cons
 ulates of Germany in Canada\, will bring together Canadian and German expe
 rts for an afternoon of conversations on water sustainability\, climate re
 silience and innovation.\nAs we look ahead to the 2026 UN Water Conference
  in Abu Dhabi\, the event will explore how emerging technologies\, data an
 d AI can contribute to more sustainable water management and strengthen in
 ternational cooperation.\nThe event will feature York University researche
 rs Satinder Kaur Brar\, Sapna Sharma and Usman Khan\, alongside Diana Nenz
  from Germany’s Federal Ministry for the Environment and Mark Fisher\, P
 resident of the Canadian Water Agency. Expert contributions will also come
  from Katherine Balpataky (DataStream)\, Henning Oppel (Okeanos)\, Heather
  Crochetiere (Foresight Canada) and Julian Klaus (University of Bonn)\, br
 inging together perspectives from research\, government\, industry and civ
 il society.\nThrough expert presentations\, panel discussions and thematic
  conversations\, participants will exchange ideas\, share perspectives and
  identify opportunities for a water-secure future.\nDate: October 27\, 202
 6Time: 1:00 pm to 4:30 pmLocation: Schulich School of Business\, York Univ
 ersity\nRSVP here\nFor more information\, please contact Ellianne Feenstra
  at ellianne@yorku.ca ( mailto:ellianne@yorku.ca ).\n \n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023
LOCATION:Executive Dining Room\, ELC | Seymour Schulich Building\, Keele C
 ampus
ORGANIZER;CN="York International":MAILTO:goglobal@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/climate-talks-water-canada-germany-road
 -to-the-un-water-conference/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
