SUMMARY:Democracy Fitness: Curiosity
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T150000
UID:6aad8a05f9ed2e003851bbe5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive\nsession. Democracy
  Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring the s
 kills that help people participate in civic life\, build understanding and
  work together.\nIn this session\, we’ll exercise our\nCuriosity\nmuscle
 s. In a democracy\, we don't know the answers in advance. If we stay open 
 and creative\, we become wiser and discover new possibilities.\nThis progr
 am is for\nadults\,\nplease register for email reminders\, drop-in's are w
 elcome.\nThis program is offered in partnership with Democracy Fitness Glo
 bal and MASS LBP.\nGenerously supported by McConnell Foundation.\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad8a05f9ed2e003851bbe5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
