BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_4h7dspldpuviiv4o1slj9o5p5c
X-SOURCE:CITA Seminars
DTSTART:20261028T174900Z
DTEND:20261028T184900Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T043526Z
UID:vtd8kilrg437otbmdv8dn7a0ts@google.com
CREATED:20261023T175043Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Title: <b>The interior of dynamical black hole</b></p>\n\n<p
 >Abstract: The celebrated singularity theorem of Penrose predicts the exist
 ence of an incomplete causal geodesic in the interior of a black hole\; how
 ever\, this situation is compatible with the absence of a curvature singula
 rity\, e.g.\, at the Cauchy horizon of a Kerr black hole.\n\nThe Strong Cos
 mic Censorship conjecture\, on the other hand\, claims the presence of a (c
 urvature) singularity generically\, which preserves the deterministic evolu
 tion of the Einstein equations: in particular\, the Kerr Cauchy horizon is 
 non-generic.\n\nWe'll review recent progress towards a proof of the conject
 ure and towards understanding gravitational collapse for rotating black hol
 es in classical gravity.</p>\n<p>Host: <b>Soumendra Kishore Roy</b></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T175043Z
LOCATION:Idealab Bridge
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Maxime Van de Moortel (University of Toronto\, Maths Department)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
