SUMMARY:Making Room: Access to Capital for Affordable Housing - by More
  Neighbours Toronto
LOCATION:It's Ok* Studios
DESCRIPTION:More info: https://luma.com/97u9gvvu\n\nHosted by More
  Neighbours Toronto (https://www.moreneighbours.ca/)\n\n​Why does
  affordable housing keep slipping through the cracks\, even when the will
  to save it exists? In this talk\, Krystal breaks down the real barriers
  standing between communities and the buildings they're trying to protect:
  financial capital\, yes\, but also the social capital and trust-building
  that often gets overlooked.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:showuptoronto_static_showupto_ics
X-SOURCE:Show Up Toronto
UID:124d0532-4f51-4101-a54e-01c5918ca6a0
CREATED:20261015T065026Z
DTSTART:20261028T230000Z
DTEND:20261029T010000Z
SUMMARY:Naza screening - by Hot Docs
LOCATION:Hot Docs
DESCRIPTION:More info:
  https://boxoffice.hotdocs.ca/websales/pages/info.aspx?evtinfo=658890%7Ecf
 285ddd-dacb-4f18-89b8-1252c6dcffa6\n\nHosted by Hot Docs
  (https://hotdocs.ca)\n\nThe directors behind Oscar-winning documentary\,
  No Other Land return with a searing film that turns its investigative
  lens to the systems behind Israel’s military campaign in Gaza.
  Clandestinely filmed at night from rooftops in Tel Aviv\, NAZA reveals
  testimony from Israeli military insiders examining how technology and
  intelligence protocols have shaped the war.
END:VEVENT
