X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Toronto Ai Machine Learning Data Science": "https://www.meetup.com/toronto-ai-machine-learning-data-science/events/316758185/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_toronto_ai_machine_learning_data_science
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto AI & ML
UID:event_316758185@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261024T043624Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T140000
SUMMARY:Oct 29 - How to Build Vision Data Agents with Tools\, Skills\, and
  MCP
DESCRIPTION:Toronto AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\nIn t
 his session\, you’ll learn how to build production-ready AI agents that 
 can reason over your data\, automate complex tasks\, and integrate seamles
 sly into your existing stack using tools\, skills\, and the Model Context 
 Protocol (MCP).\n\n**Date\, Time and Location**\n\nOct 29\, 2026\n9:00 AM 
 - 10:00 AM PST\nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/eve
 nts/how-to-build-vision-data-agents-with-tools-skills-and-mcp-october-29-2
 026)**\n\nWe’ll walk through how modern agentic systems move beyond simp
 le prompts—leveraging structured tools like dataset operations\, embeddi
 ngs\, evaluation pipelines\, and model execution to take real action. You
 ’ll see how these agents can tag data\, run inference\, evaluate perform
 ance\, and surface insights automatically\, all within a unified workflow.
 \n\nBy combining natural language interfaces with programmable building bl
 ocks\, teams can dramatically reduce manual effort\, accelerate experiment
 ation\, and unlock faster decision-making across the ML lifecycle.\n\nWhet
 her you're building data-centric AI systems\, managing large-scale vision 
 datasets\, or exploring agentic workflows for the first time\, this sessio
 n will give you a practical blueprint for getting started.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-ai-machine-learning-data-scie
 nce/events/316758185/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260928T231506Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T231506Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
