X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/disaster-seminar-series-five-things-id-tell-my-2018-self-reflections-on-building-a-career-in-health-emergency-management/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Disaster Seminar Series: Five Things I’d Tell My 2018 Self: Refl
 ections on Building a Career in Health Emergency Management
DTSTART:20261029T184500Z
DTEND:20261029T194500Z
DTSTAMP:20261019T210300Z
UID:MEC-a3577dabfbc7a0e6685b1a3b68a0ac84@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261029T184500Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change,Faculty of Health,
 Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Las
 sonde School of Engineering,Y-EMERGE
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261019
DESCRIPTION:Join Y-EMERGE for our ongoing Disaster Seminar Series. This se
 ssion will feature Moira Hennebury\, Manager of Emergency Preparedness at 
 Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre.\nAbstract: When Moira Hennebury complet
 ed York University’s Master of Disaster and Emergency Management program
  in December 2018\, she was just beginning to envision what a career in em
 ergency management could look like. Since then\, she has progressed from i
 ntern to analyst\, specialist\, and manager\, supporting dozens of emergen
 cy responses and leading high-impact preparedness initiatives across Ontar
 io’s health sector.\nToday\, Moira leads the Emergency Preparedness team
  at Sunnybrook\, a nationally leading and globally recognized academic hea
 lth sciences centre\, and home to Canada’s first and largest trauma cent
 re. Most recently\, she provided leadership for health and medical plannin
 g in support of Toronto’s hosting of the FIFA World Cup 2026™. Drawing
  on lessons learned throughout her career journey\, Moira will share five 
 insights she wishes she had known when starting out in the profession. The
  session will explore how emergency management theory translates into prac
 tice\, the skills and experiences that matter most in an increasingly comp
 lex and evolving field\, and the realities of building a meaningful career
 . Through these reflections\, Moira will offer lessons for emerging profes
 sionals while highlighting what has sustained her passion for healthcare e
 mergency management over the past eight years.\nFor more information on th
 e weekly Disaster Seminar Series visit the website: https://www.yorku.ca/r
 esearch/yemerge/disaster-seminar-series/ ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/y
 emerge/disaster-seminar-series/ )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261019
LOCATION:109 Atkinson Building (Harry Crowe Room) @ 4700 Keele Street\, Yo
 rk University\, North York\, ON M3J 1P3\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN=ORU-Y-EMERGE:MAILTO:yemerge@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/disaster-seminar-series-five-things-id-
 tell-my-2018-self-reflections-on-building-a-career-in-health-emergency-man
 agement/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
