X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-breaking-into-accounting-careers-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Mentor Circles | Breaking into Accounting Careers
DTSTART:20261029T213000Z
DTEND:20261029T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261016T200200Z
UID:MEC-b520fbfb0d37fbb44382ab286af16a50@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261029T213000Z
SEQUENCE:26
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/1
 2/Mentor-Circles-1.png
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Advising,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Prof
 essional Studies,Schulich School of Business
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261016
DESCRIPTION:Explore accounting career paths and CPA requirements in this i
 nteractive in-person mentoring session. Learn how to choose your path and 
 adapt to technology-driven changes in the profession.\nDate: Thursday\, Oc
 t. 29\nTime: 5:30 – 7 p.m.\nLocation: Zoom webinar\n\nAlamgir Khandwala 
 (BAS ’17)\, Revenue Accounting Manager\, Uber\nAlam Khandwala is a finan
 ce and systems leader working at the intersection of Finance\, Systems\, O
 perations\, and Product. Based in the San Francisco Bay Area\, he is curre
 ntly an accounting manager on Uber’s Global Revenue team\, with previous
  experience at Deloitte and Moneris spanning public and corporate accounti
 ng\, finance transformation\, systems\, and emerging technologies. Beyond 
 his accounting career\, Alam serves as global chair of Able@Uber\, Uber’
 s employee resource group focused on disability inclusion and accessibilit
 y. He is also a published peer-reviewed author\, with research exploring t
 he intersection of artificial intelligence\, pain\, and medicine.\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\nThijith Vidanagamage\, CPA (BBA ’21\, MACC ’22)\, Auditor\, Canad
 a Revenue Agency\n\n\n\n\nThijith Vidanagamage is a chartered professional
  accountant currently working as an income tax auditor at the Canada Reven
 ue Agency. He graduated from the Schulich School of Business with a Bachel
 or of Business Administration (BBA) and a Master of Accounting (MAcc). Ove
 r the past four years\, he has gained experience in different areas of tax
 ation\, working with businesses across various industries. Having earned h
 is CPA designation\, he looks forward to sharing his experiences and advic
 e with students interested in pursuing accounting.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016
ORGANIZER;CN="Office of Alumni Engagement":MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-breaking-into-accounting
 -careers-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
