X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Tockify Torevent": "https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/24077/1793376000000"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tockify_torevent
X-SOURCE:Toronto Events (Tockify)
UID:TKF/6755f42da02aaf1c2599e7ae/24077/29889600/0/0
DTSTART:20261030T160000Z
DTEND:20261030T210000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/24077/1793376000000
SUMMARY: Cylinder Spectrum & Polygon Plexus
DESCRIPTION:"Cylinder Spectrum" & "Polygon Plexus" are two visual art exh
 ibitions by Toronto artist Angela Julian (Native Torontonian and OCADU gr
 aduate). Both shows are located inside the Sun Gallery at 918 Bathurst Ar
 ts & Culture Center. The collected works are a group of large scale color
 ful abstract paintings done in plaster. They range in size\, scale\, shap
 e\, and number\, but they are all tied together through the mediums of pl
 aster and acrylic paint.\n\n\nOn one side of the gallery is the show "Cyl
 inder Spectrum"\, which is a group of acrylic paintings done on distinctl
 y rounded canvases that were covered in layers of mixed-media and plaster
 . These are shown both as individual works and presented as a group that 
 makeup a larger installation. The circular nature of the canvases and sur
 faces links the entire show by their rounded nature. On the opposite side
  of the gallery is the show "Polygon Plexus" which is a group of hand-mad
 e canvases and surfaces that were created to form irregular shapes. These
  outer shapes are deliberately jagged\, pointed\, elongated\, and heavily
  textured surfaces\, and each painting is covered with a either a geometr
 ic or abstract pattern. Both exhibitions demonstrate a variety of differe
 nt color schemes and embrace vibrant\, highly-saturated colors.\n\n\nThe 
 Sun Gallery is the twin space to the Star Gallery on the property\, and i
 t is an airy and brilliantly lit space with wide sky-lights that allow fo
 r beautiful natural day-light. The gallery space is located at 918 Bathur
 st Arts & Culture Center in the Annex neighborhood (Bloor / Bathurst area
 ). The center is a historic building in Toronto and was formerly a Buddhi
 st Temple before it became a venue for Arts and Culture. It has an in-hou
 se audience that ranges from both broad to local. With many disappearing 
 gallery spaces in Toronto\, it proudly boasts its survival and longevity 
 as a space within the landscape of an ever-changing metropolis city. The 
 interior of 918 Bathurst is a mix of modern design elements in conjunctio
 n with its preserved historic architecture\, notably the beautiful wooden
  beams of its ceilings. These are two very fun shows and run until the en
 d of October\, 2026.\n\nUpcoming Events | 918 Bathurst Centre for Culture
 \, Arts\, Media and Education https://www.918bathurst.com/events
CATEGORIES:Art-Show/Gallery-Event,918-Bathurst-Arts-and-Culture-Center
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6ad3e61762b7c5607c7bf5bc/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:"Cylinder Spectrum" & "Polygon Plexus" are two visua
 l art exhibitions by Toronto artist Angela Julian (Native Torontonian and
  OCADU graduate). Both shows are...
LOCATION:918 Bathurst Arts and Culture Center\,918 Bathurst St\, Toronto\
 , ON M5R 3G5\, Canada
CREATED:20261017T213519Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T043646Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T213519Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Tockify Torevent": "https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/24078/1793376000000"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tockify_torevent
X-SOURCE:Toronto Events (Tockify)
UID:TKF/6755f42da02aaf1c2599e7ae/24078/29889600/0/0
DTSTART:20261030T160000Z
DTEND:20261030T210000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/24078/1793376000000
SUMMARY: The Face is a Landscape
DESCRIPTION:"The Face is a Landscape" is a visual arts exhibition by Toro
 nto artist Angela Julian. The large body of art features colorful works d
 one in Portraiture. The show is comprised of drawings and paintings creat
 ed in a highly-detailed contemporary style. She explores painterly and dr
 awn techniques in both wet and dry mediums. The faces are designed using 
 many layers of blended line-work\, impressions\, and cross-hatchings. She
  uses very fine brushes and drawing instruments to achieve these micro-te
 chniques that makeup the broader whole of the picture. The works are loca
 ted in the Star Gallery and fill up the room from floor to ceiling. The s
 ubjects of each portrait are all well-known authors\, writers\, or philos
 ophers by nature. Angela is penning her first book series in the high-fan
 tasy genre\, she has included portraits in the show based on writers that
  had a direct impact on her as a reader and aspiring author. The exhibiti
 on is largely a homage to those writers and thinkers who influenced her.\
 n\n\nThe Star Gallery is located at 918 Bathurst Arts & Culture Center in
  the Annex neighborhood (Bloor / Bathurst area). The center is a historic
  building in Toronto and was formerly a Buddhist Temple before it became 
 a venue for Arts and Culture. It has an in-house audience that ranges fro
 m both broad to local. With many disappearing gallery spaces in Toronto\,
  it proudly boasts its survival and longevity as a space within the lands
 cape of an ever-changing metropolis city. The interior of 918 Bathurst is
  a mix of modern design elements in conjunction with its preserved histor
 ic architecture\, notably its beautiful wooden ceilings. The show runs un
 til the end of October 2026\, don't miss it!
