SUMMARY:Excel Basics 1: Create a Simple Spreadsheet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261101T153000
UID:6aac7b2ca5dbde002aa56717@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for absolute beginner
 s with little or no Excel experience.\nIn this first session\, you will:\n
 Learn the basic function and design of Excel files\nPractice basic data en
 try for text\, numbers\, and basic functions: Sum\, AutoSum and Average\nC
 reate and save your first workbook and worksheets\nUpon completion of this
  class\, you will be able to use Excel at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: B
 asic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demons
 trations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac7b2ca5dbde002aa56717
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
