SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T153000
UID:6ac7bdf4ebad22004543f2ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto has one of the largest urban forests in the world. Joi
 n the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for an in-library presentation 
 on this amazing natural habitat that reaches all corners of Toronto.\nWe
 ’ll discuss what makes the urban forest so special and share tools to he
 lp you explore and understand it better. Bring questions and curiosities\,
  and leave with greater confidence and a deeper understanding of your City
  and the natural world around you!\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fra
 gile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Libra
 ry\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Northern District\, MFPR
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7bdf4ebad22004543f2ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
