SUMMARY:Word Basics 2: Format a Flyer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T153000
UID:6aa1ad3ef9ed2e00384f52dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build on your basic Microsoft Word skills and learn to use Wor
 d more effectively.\nIn this class\, you will:\nPractice new Word skills w
 hile      you design a flyer\nFormat text\, margins\, indents\,      heade
 rs and footers\nFormat text as columns\nCreate bulleted\, numbered and    
   sorted lists\nReview your document with      Spelling and Grammar check 
 and Thesaurus\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to use eve
 n more Word tools to design your documents.\nPrerequisites:\nWord Basics 1
  or equivalent skills. Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nForma
 t: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1ad3ef9ed2e00384f52dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
