SUMMARY:Our Fragile Planet: Growing Native Plants from Seed
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T190000
UID:6acfe339f34d34366b3cf7ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Growing native plants from seed is an inexpensive and easy way
  to add plants to your garden – but you need to start early! Many native
  plants require several months of cold temperatures to sprout in the sprin
 g.\nJoin this session with\nToronto Master Gardeners\nto learn where to ge
 t your seed and how to sow it over the winter for germination in the sprin
 g.\nAt the end of the program\, native seeds will be given out to attendee
 s\, while supplies last.\nSuitable for gardeners of any skill level\, with
  any kind of outdoor space.\nDrop-in. No registration required.\nThis prog
 ram is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Fr
 iends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Rexdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6acfe339f34d34366b3cf7ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
