DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T150000
UID:6ac3fa91c6cddb004595bb06@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Planting bulbs in the fall will bring glorious rewards in your
  spring garden. A Toronto Master Gardener will give advice on what to plan
 t\, how to plant them and yes\, even a few pointers on squirrels! At the e
 nd of the program\, bulbs will be given out to attendees\,\nwhile supplies
  last\n.\nSuitable for gardeners of any skill level\, with any kind of out
 door space.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
