BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad0e8de96ec3a003adabdcb"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Make A Will with the Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T150000
UID:6ad0e8de96ec3a003adabdcb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month and TPL is delighted to host the
  Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will and 
 powers of attorney for you and your family.\nA member of the Ontario Bar 
 Association who practices Trusts and Estates Law will speak about the elem
 ents of a will\, what happens if you don’t have one\, what are powers of
  attorney\, why they are important and special considerations to keep in m
 ind when preparing your estate and care plans.\nNote\, this program is for
  general information only\, not for drafting individual wills.\nDrop-in\, 
 no registration required
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad0e8de96ec3a003adabdcb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
