SUMMARY:Early Modern Philosophy Research Interest Group (Aman Sahkardande\, U of T)
DESCRIPTION:The Early Modern Philosophy Research Interest Group welcomes Aman Sahkardande\, a PhD student in the department working on phenomenology and 17th- and 18th-century European philosophy. Historically\, his research focuses on the work of Immanuel Kant\, Edmund Husserl\, and Martin Heidegger. Philosophically\, he is interested in what studying experience (cognitive\, perceptual\, practical\, etc.) can tell us about the world\, and in particular what it can tell us about the kinds of beings that we (humans) are. \nTalk Title\nTBD \nTalk Abstract\nTBD
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/early-modern-philosophy-research-interest-group-aman-sahkardande-u-of-t/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Aman-resized.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Tarek Dika":MAILTO:tarek.dika@utoronto.ca
END:VEVENT
