SUMMARY:Make A Will with the Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T140000
UID:6ada5191e06996003a854142@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month and TPL is delighted to host the
  Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will and 
 powers of attorney for you and your family. Margaret E. Rintoul\, a member
  of the\nOntario Bar Association\nwho practices Trusts and Estates Law wil
 l speak about the elements of a will\, what happens if you don’t have on
 e\, what are powers of attorney\, why they are important and special consi
 derations to keep in mind when preparing your estate and care plans.\nNote
 \, this program is for general information only\, not for drafting individ
 ual wills.\nRegistration is prioritized. Drop-in if space permitting.\nLiv
 e or automated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, interven
 or services\, or attendant services are available upon request. Please sub
 mit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-even
 ts. ​​
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada5191e06996003a854142
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
