SEQUENCE:26
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 08/Photo20_James-Robertson-1-Analyze-your-Assi_James-Robertson-9-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Community Hub,LA&amp\;PS Founder
 s College,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS 
 Student Success,LA&amp\;PS Students All,LA&amp\;PS Students-International,
 LA&amp\;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,LA&amp\;PS Writing
  Centre
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260827
DESCRIPTION:Understand your professor’s expectations. Start brainstormin
 g and formulate a plan.\nThe Write Now! series consists of four workshops\
 , each of which focuses on one aspect of the writing process:\nWorkshop 1:
  Analyze Your Assignment\nWorkshop 2: Construct an Argument\nWorkshop 3: M
 eaningful Citations\nWorkshop 4: Effective Editing\nAt the end of each wor
 kshop\, you’ll receive access to a quiz\, which you will need to complet
 e within 72 hours of the workshop date. If you pass the quiz\, you will re
 ceive a badge\, which will be recorded on the Write Now! eClass site.\nIf 
 you attend all four workshops and pass each workshop’s quiz within one a
 cademic calendar year\, you’ll attain a Certificate of Completion that c
 an be added to your resume and professional networking sites\, such as Lin
 kedIn.\nRegister Now\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928
ORGANIZER;CN="James Robertson":MAILTO:jroberts@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/analyze-your-assignment-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
