UID:6ac2ad9f901b02002cc00b75@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Elders of the 2SLGBTQ+ community\, this space is for you! Join
  us for two sessions\, make your own Zine\, and leave with 10 copies to gi
 ve to family and friends.\nBasic supplies including collage materials will
  be provided\, but community members are encouraged to bring personal memo
 rabilia they want to include\, such as things like photos\, drawings\, ti
 ckets\, news clippings\, pressed flowers\, and other ephemera.\nCommunity 
 allies are welcome. Light refreshments will be provided.\nRegistration i
 s recommended. Drop-in space will be available until room capacity is reac
 hed.\nInformation Collection Notice: The personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Bagshaw Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac2ad9f901b02002cc00b75
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
