SUMMARY:Turning Red Flags into Strengths: How to Answer Tough Interview Qu
 estions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T180000
UID:6ab45d7fda318a10e63655ea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Tough interview questions can make even strong candidates seco
 nd-guess themselves. This practical workshop helps participants identify t
 he experiences that may feel difficult to explain in an interview and lear
 n how to present them with confidence and clarity. Through common intervie
 w scenarios\, participants will practice reframing gaps\, career changes\,
  weaknesses\, and 'lack of canadian experience' into credible stories that
  highlight their strengths\, learning and growth.\nThis program is part of
  TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead
  donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, F
 riends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nThe William and Nona
  Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careerco
 ach\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Zoom webinar\
 n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab45d7fda318a10e63655ea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/john-burge/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Common Hour: Celebrating the Canadian League of Composers: John Bu
 rge\, Piano
DTSTART:20261112T173000Z
DTEND:20261112T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260925T190600Z
UID:MEC-81190ee016c56828c2f2c3f2cd94db77@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261112T173000Z
SEQUENCE:23
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/johnburge.jpg
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260925
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of the Canadian League of Composers 75th Annive
 rsary in 2026\, composer and pianist\, John Burge presents a solo piano re
 cital of music composed by many of the CLC past presidents. Starting with 
 music by founding President\, John Weinzweig\, the program proceeds chrono
 logically to current president\, Tyler Versluis. The concert opens with a 
 musical land acknowledgement\, “Trillium\,” composed by Indigenous-Can
 adian composer and CLC member\, Beverley McKiver\, and concludes with a ro
 using collective singing of O Canada. This all-Canadian concert promises t
 o be an event of historical\, cultural and artistic significance.\nThursda
 y\, November 12\, 2026\n12:30 – 1:30 p.m. \nTribute Communities Recital
  Hall\nFREE\nComposer and pianist\, John Burge ( https://sdm.queensu.ca/pe
 ople/burge-john )\, taught at Queen’s University\, Kingston\, Ontario\, 
 for 38 years before retiring as a Professor Emeritus in 2025. Many of Burg
 e’s orchestral works\, such as Snowdrift\, The Canadian Shield and Rocky
  Mountain Overture\, have been performed by orchestras across Canada and i
 nternationally. His string orchestra work\, Flanders Fields Reflections\, 
 as recorded by Sinfonia Toronto\, received the 2009 Juno Award for the Bes
 t Canadian Classical Composition. In 2014 he was inducted into the Royal S
 ociety of Canada for his achievements as a composer and support of the Art
 s in Canada. Having completed his Associate Diploma from the Royal Conserv
 atory of Toronto in Piano Performance while still in high school\, John Bu
 rge has continued to perform throughout his career\, usually in presentati
 ons of his own music. Over the years\, his piano music has been included i
 n a number of conservatory music syllabi and he is in high demand as a mus
 ic festival adjudicator. A passionate advocate for Canadian music\, he ser
 ved on the executive committee of the Canadian League of Composers from 19
 93-2007 (including eight years as President) and on the SOCAN Foundation b
 oard of directors from 2009-2025\, as well as on the boards of several art
 s organizations in the Kingston area.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall\, 112 Accolade East Building\, Y
 ork University
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/john-burge/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
