SUMMARY:Garden with Purpose: Practical Ecological Gardening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T200000
UID:6ad2551bde300e00451adabf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You have the power to create real ecological change — right 
 in your own backyard. In this introductory program\, discover the core pri
 nciples of ecological gardening and learn how to transform your garden int
 o a space that’s both environmentally responsible and visually stunning.
 \nA Toronto Master Gardener will provide guidance on how to create habitat
 \, manage water wisely\, and reduce your ecological impact — all while c
 ultivating a landscape rich with beauty and year-round interest.\nSuitable
  for gardeners of any skill level\, with any kind of outdoor space.\nThis 
 program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported b
 y Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad2551bde300e00451adabf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
