SUMMARY:Google Docs 1: Create and Edit a File
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T153000
UID:6aac7b448cf597003f94a646@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how Google Docs can be a useful free tool when you don't
  have access to Microsoft Word. In this introductory class you will learn 
 how to open\, create\, save and delete Google Docs. Features such as highl
 ight\, bold\, italics\, underline\, font colour and font size will be cove
 red as well as how to use spell check\, print\, and download as Word docum
 ent.\nPrerequisites: Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFormat
 : Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 
 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac7b448cf597003f94a646
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac902fa295b3b0033cb0d5a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) for Healthy Aging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T163000
UID:6ac902fa295b3b0033cb0d5a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for anyone looking to strengthen their well-being
 —whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or s
 imply wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. The WRA
 P for Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Workshop for Healthy Aging is e
 xpertly designed by Hope + Me for individuals aged 60 and older using the 
 principles of WRAP\, but with scenarios and tools focused on common aging 
 challenges.\nThis 3-week session is appropriate for people with no experie
 nce with WRAP\, or for those who wish to refresh their knowledge and skill
 s.\nParticipants will receive a certificate of participation upon program 
 completion\, but these sessions do not contribute to a WRAP certificate. F
 ind more WRAP program options at TPL\nhere.\nThis WRAP Group meets every S
 unday\, once a week for 3 weeks November 8 - November 22. Week 1 will be 
 3 hours\, with a 30 minute overview and orientation of  WRAP\; Weeks 2 and
  3 will be 2.5 hours.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided\n.\nSnacks and 
 refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be
  available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nHope 
 + Me\n. Hope + Me is solely responsible for the protection of personal inf
 ormation collected through the program registration process.
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac902fa295b3b0033cb0d5a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
