DESCRIPTION:Hello everyone\,\nWe are pleased to invite you to a special bo
 ok talk featuring Crystal Gail Fraser and Sara Komarnisky\, authors of the
  national bestseller Talk Treaty to Me: Understanding the Basics of Treati
 es and Land in Canada.\nJoin us for a dialogue and Q&A with the authors as
  they discuss their book and explore the basics of treaties and land in Ca
 nada. Copies of the book will also be available for purchase.\nEvent Detai
 ls:\n📅 Tuesday\, November 24\, 2026\n🕙 10:00–11:30 AM\n📍 George
  Spragge Classroom\, Archives of Ontario\n134 Ian MacDonald Blvd\nThe even
 t is free and open to the public. Please RSVP by November 14. Light refres
 hments will be served.\nRSVP: https://forms.gle/zf7rTVbJKR6uRqvA8\nAs part
  of the event\, the Archives of Ontario will display Treaty 9.\nWe hope yo
 u can join us for this engaging conversation!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261013
LOCATION:Archives of Ontario - York University @ 134 Ian MacDonald Blvd\, 
 North York\, ON M3J 2S5\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Centre for Indigenous Knowledges and Languages":MAILTO:cikl@
 yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/talk-treaty-to-me-book-event/
