SUMMARY:Rainbow Seniors’ Social: Everyday Art\, An Evaluation of our Vis
 ual Literacy with Ali Zargari Ouroozaki
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T153000
UID:6ad6a7b996ec3a003adba8b4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Elders of the 2SLGBTQ+ community\, this space is for you! Join
  us for three workshops facilitated by the artist Ali Zargari Ouroozaki\, 
 and expand your ability to understand\, appreciate\, and create art.\nEach
  session takes a different focus\, beginning with understanding the primar
 y elements of visual art\, then analyzing their interrelations\, and final
 ly understanding their material properties. Participants will have the opp
 ortunity to apply these lessons with their own creations.\nCommunity allie
 s are welcome. All necessary art supplies as well as light refreshments wi
 ll be provided.\nRegistration is recommended\n. Drop-in space will be avai
 lable until room capacity is reached.\nThursday\, November 19\nth\n& 26\nt
 h\n\; December 3\nrd\n\, 2:30-3:30pm.\nInformation Collection Notice: The 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad6a7b996ec3a003adba8b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
