SUMMARY:Toronto Master Gardeners: Growing Native Plants from Seed
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T140000
UID:6aca4bf0ea50a10050a6cfb9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Growing native plants from seed is an inexpensive and easy way
  to add plants to your garden – but many native plants require several m
 onths of cold temperatures to sprout in the spring. A\nToronto Master Gard
 ener\nwill go over where to get your seed and how to sow it over the winte
 r for germination in the spring. At the end of the program\, native seeds 
 will be given out to attendees\, while supplies last. Suitable for gardene
 rs of any skill level\, with any kind of outdoor space.\nThis program is p
 art of TPL's Our Fragile Planet program series\, supported by Friends of T
 oronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nRegister online or call 416-396-39
 75.\n-----\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aca4bf0ea50a10050a6cfb9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
