DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T143000
UID:6adb9750e06996003a8576c8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month.\nLearn how to take contr
 ol of your finances and make your money work for you. This practical works
 hop facilitated by a Financial empowerment staff member from North York Co
 mmunity House will help you understand your income and expenses\, create a
  realistic budget\, start saving and learn how to access government benefi
 ts you may be eligible for\, helping you build a stronger and more secure 
 financial foundation.\nOne-on-one support is available at select branches.
  Meet with Financial Empowerment staff for free financial counselling. Boo
 k your free appointment today. Speak with branch staff or visit\ntpl.ca/fi
 nancial-empowerment\nfor more information.
LOCATION:Albion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adb9750e06996003a8576c8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
