SUMMARY: FUSION LAB STAGED READING
DESCRIPTION:Since 2021\, the Fusion Festival has brought together writers
 \, directors and actors to workshop and develop new works by Canadian pla
 ywrights & screenwriters. Building on this tradition\, we’re proud to int
 roduce The Fusion Lab\, a new initiative dedicated to supporting Canadian
  artists through year-round workshops designed to facilitate the creation
  of new Canadian works. The program will provide opportunities for artist
 s to develop their work\, with selected scripts showcase at our annual Fu
 sion Festival!\n\nThis season\, we’re excited to present staged readings 
 of two original Canadian plays written by Brandon Nicoletti.\n\nSPOTTER\n
 \nFeaturing: Patrick S. McEwen &amp\; Blake Pyne\n\nWhen Kai nearly injur
 es himself during a bench press\, Tyler steps in and offers to be his spo
 tter. The two men form an unlikely connection that sparks conversations a
 bout body image\, modern dating\, and the way gay men see each other.\n\n
 KILL TEST\n\nFeaturing: Marisa Roggeveen\, Andy Kalirai\, & Scott Clark\n
 \nA rookie operative must extract information from a captive while her me
 ntor tests her resolve.\n\nJoin us at Naturlandia on November 27 th at 8:
 30pm for an evening of new Canadian theatre.\n\nCome experience original 
 storytelling\, support emerging Canadian artists\, and help us continue o
 ur tradition of bringing bold new orks to the stage and screen!\n\nTICKET
 S: www.tickettailor.com/events/blackalloyproductions/2340540 https://www.
 tickettailor.com/events/blackalloyproductions/2340540
CATEGORIES:Dance---Performance---Theatre,Naturlandia
