DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T120000
UID:6ad125b3a85a2c00337fcb96@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expr
 essions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past\, craftsmen had an ex
 tensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays\, we tend to rely heavil
 y on tools such as a protractors\, compasses\, and rulers. In this worksho
 p\, participants will be guided through step-by-step instructions using d
 rawing tools and watercolour paint to create their own geometric pattern 
 and complex design art pieces.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad125b3a85a2c00337fcb96
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
