SUMMARY:Festival Select: The Swimmer (Frank Perry\, 1968)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T203000
UID:6ad0d4569d27a000455116db@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the Society and Recreation department of the North York C
 entral Library for monthly screenings of fiction and non-fiction films tha
 t push the boundaries of the medium. This month we are showing Frank Perry
 's\nThe Swimmer\n(1968).\nSynopsis (ACF Films): Neddy Merrill has been aw
 ay for most of the Summer. He reappears at a [friend's] pool. As they talk
 \, someone notices that there are pools spanning the entire valley. He [de
 cides] to jog from pool to pool to swim the whole valley. As he stops in e
 ach pool his interactions tell his life story.\nNo registration required.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad0d4569d27a000455116db
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
