BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7c686fee2d21deb249a7a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Design a Holiday Tote Bag
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T113000
UID:6ad7c686fee2d21deb249a7a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Let your imagination run wild using the tote bag as your blank
  canvas. Create a custom tote bag for yourself or for a loved one as a hol
 iday gift. All materials will be provided\, including fabric paints\, fabr
 ic markers\, stencils\, and one tote bag per person.\nLimited spots availa
 ble. Registration required.\n** Please arrive on time. Registered spots wi
 ll be given away 5 minutes after the program starts. **\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First Floor Program Room (CPR)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7c686fee2d21deb249a7a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab7053e31e9a41a0fbc9480"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Creative Connections: Activities for Creative & Social Connections
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T113000
UID:6ab7053e31e9a41a0fbc9480@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for creative group activities that support mental well
 ness\, social connection and a sense of belonging. Enjoy music\, movement\
 , mindfulness and more while connecting with others and engaging with your
  community.\nDrop-in\, no registration is required.\nTTC Presto tickets wi
 ll be provided upon request.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all
  participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis 
 program is in collaboration with\nCanadian Mental Health Association Toron
 to\n.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room\, Basement Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab7053e31e9a41a0fbc9480
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
