SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T200000
UID:6abfc99029c3d600332d2c3d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC)\nworkshop is unlike any oth
 er. We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\,
  listen deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into 
 your story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\,
  and respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials ar
 e provided. Workshops are not sequential\; every workshop is unique - join
  in at any session and let's write together!\nDrop in\, no registration re
 quired\n. Please arrive a few minutes early. For more information\, please
  contact the branch.\n​Presented by Writers Collective of Canada (WCC)\,
  a charitable arts-health organization that ignites connection through cre
 ativity by inspiring powerful\, authentic stories shared in community.\nht
 tps://wcc-cec.org/
LOCATION:Evelyn Gregory
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfc99029c3d600332d2c3d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Build Your First App with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T200000
UID:6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop with our 
 Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll use an AI coding assistant
  to build your own small\, useful webpage\, checklist\, or organizer from 
 scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe what you want\, review the 
 plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bugs\, and write documentatio
 n so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, key
 boarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experien
 ce required.\nRegistration is required and will start November 9\, 2026 at
  12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the 
 start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on
  a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you wish 
 to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own USB s
 tick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes acti
 vities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou d
 o not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are 
 encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which
  include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the priva
 cy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\n
 Learn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Antigravity\nLear
 n more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more
  about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
