X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Quilting Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T200000
UID:6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The focus of this program is to make quilts for donation\, usi
 ng fabrics that have been donated to the group for this purpose.\nParticip
 ants meet weekly to share ideas and inspiration while working on quilts. T
 here are no sewing machines at the library so any sewing is done by hand. 
 Most participants also work on quilts using their own sewing machine at ho
 me. Quilts are completed both as individual projects and as group collabor
 ations.\nNew members are welcome\, and will have access to the instruction
 s\, fabrics\, needle and thread required to contribute on-site to the curr
 ent group project.\nRegarding dates: The quilters will not meet when schoo
 l is out. E.g. March break and during the summer (July and August) and dur
 ing December break.
LOCATION:Jones
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Preschool": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac5874da85a2c00337db3b3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_preschool
SUMMARY:Classical & Latin American Guitar Performance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T193000
UID:6ac5874da85a2c00337db3b3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Karla García is a Chilean-Canadian guitarist\, music creator\
 , and educator based in Toronto. Originally from Chiloé\, Chile\, she ha
 s performed as a soloist and collaborator with orchestras and ensembles in
  Canada and Latin America. Her musical work brings together classical guit
 ar\, Latin American music\, popular music\, and original songs. Karla stud
 ied guitar at the University of Chile and has performed with orchestras in
 cluding the Ontario Pops Orchestra and the Scarborough Philharmonic Orches
 tra. As an educator\, she is passionate about creating welcoming and engag
 ing learning experiences that help students develop confidence and a lasti
 ng connection with music.\nNo registration required\, all are welcome\n!
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac5874da85a2c00337db3b3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
