SUMMARY:LinkedIn for Beginners: Build Your Profile\, Grow Your Network
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T140000
UID:6ada37b511bbf300684cef48@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to LinkedIn or not sure how to use it effectively? Learn h
 ow to create a professional profile that highlights your skills\, experien
 ces\, and strengths. This workshop will cover the basics of building your 
 online presence\, connecting with professionals\, and using LinkedIn to ex
 plore career paths\, discover opportunities\, and grow your network with c
 onfidence.\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and 
 is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with su
 pporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, Sout
 h Chapter and The William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more informati
 on\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada37b511bbf300684cef48
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
