DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T190000
UID:6ad68370377296003a4d1776@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to use Onshape\, a beginner-friendly 3D modeling pro
 gram\, to design your own custom hook! Explore the basics of 3D design as 
 you create a functional hook suited to your needs. Once your design is com
 plete\, library staff will 3D print it for you to pick up at a later date.
  Whether you're new to 3D modeling or curious about how 3D printing works\
 , this is a great opportunity to explore digital design and bring your ide
 as to life.\nAges 18 and up\nRegistration begins November 25 at 9:00 am.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Inside the DIH
