BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Philosophy": "https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/aesthetics-reading-group-alexandra-king-simon-fraser-university/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:philosophy
X-SOURCE:UofT Philosophy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T170000
DTSTAMP:20260916T193310Z
CREATED:20260916T193310Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260916T193310Z
UID:35843-1796914800-1796922000@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Aesthetics Reading Group (Alexandra King\, Simon Fraser University)
DESCRIPTION:The Aesthetics Reading Group is pleased to welcome as guest speaker Alexandra King\, associate professor in the Department of Philosophy at Simon Fraser University. Currently\, she is thinking through what aesthetic normativity looks like: the shape it takes\, its parallels and interactions with other varieties of normativity (like the moral and epistemic)\, and whether it can be said to exist at all. Within aesthetics\, she is also interested in an assortment of issues\, including subtlety\, high and low art\, aesthetic/artistic agency\, and applied arts. She also owns\, runs\, and regularly writes for the aesthetics and philosophy of art blog Aesthetics for Birds\, which aims to make concepts and arguments in academic aesthetics accessible to a wide\, public audience. \nTalk Title\nTBA \nTalk Abstract\nTBA
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/aesthetics-reading-group-alexandra-king-simon-fraser-university/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/alex-king.png
END:VEVENT
