SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T110000
UID:6a9489c960ccaf01c02227af@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect matches older adults with a teen volunteer t
 o provide tech help\, under the guidance of library staff. Learn the basic
 s of using computers\, tablets and smartphones and popular websites and so
 ftware.\nSeniors\, please register. Drop-in may be allowed while there are
  enough volunteers available.\nIf you're a teen between the ages of 13-17 
 and would like to learn more about becoming a Seniors E-Connect volunteer\
 , visit the\nSeniors E-Connect Volunteering page\nor contact the branch.\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9489c960ccaf01c02227af
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
