SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Cuban and Brazillian Drumming
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T180000
UID:6adbc92b035faf0033de9a42@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A lively drumming program highlighting two of the most influen
 tial countries in world music\, Cuba and Brazil\, both culturally rich in 
 rhythms and songs. Experience the exciting music of traditional cultural e
 vents like Carnival and community festivals led by ​professional drummer
  and percussionist\, Joaquin Hidalgo.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub s
 ervice. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the
  summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious sna
 cks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the br
 anch to find out more.\nThe Mount Dennis Youth Hub is for youth that are 1
 3-17 years old in grades 8-12.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adbc92b035faf0033de9a42
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
