BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac53584901b02002cc07d03"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f8a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T150000
UID:6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f8a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nOctober 7:\nSingi
 n' in the Rain\nOctober 14:\nCoco\nOctober 21:\nThe Social Network\nOctobe
 r 28:\nThe King's Speech\nNovember 4:\nEternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mi
 nd\nNovember 11:\nLady Bird\nNovember 18:\nJuno\nNovember 25:\nThe Breakfa
 st Club\nDecember 2:\nMy Cousin Vinny\nDecember 9:\nSecondhand Lions\nDece
 mber 16:\nBlack Swan\nDecember 23:\nScrooged\nDecember 30:\nThe Pursuit of
  Happyness\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments ar
 e provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at th
 e program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre'
 s F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f8a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 School Age": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad8c120377296003a4d772b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_school_age
SUMMARY:Nintendo Switch Gaming
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T140000
UID:6ad8c120377296003a4d772b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy ridiculously fun multiplayer games with friends!\nRegist
 ration begins one month before program date. For ages 6 - 12.\nDrop-in's 
 welcome\, depending on program capacity.\nInformation Collection Notice:\n
 The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public L
 ibrary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d)
 . The information will only be used for event and program registration\, d
 elivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your infor
 mation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3
 97-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, New Programming Space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad8c120377296003a4d772b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a906ac836204e08fbb79755"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Wednesday Knit & Crochet Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T150000
UID:6a906ac836204e08fbb79755@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn how to knit or crochet with a fun group of peopl
 e? Looking for help with your project?\nYou can also share your projects w
 ith others\, teach or learn a technique\, and enjoy great conversation.\nA
 ll levels of expertise are welcome.\nBring your own yarn\, needles\, and c
 rochet hooks.\nDrop-in only.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a906ac836204e08fbb79755
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac94070ebad2200454442ac"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Adult Crafternoon Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T153000
UID:6ac94070ebad2200454442ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us every month at the College/Shaw Library for our Adult
  Crafternoon Social!\nDrop in for some coffee and light music while explor
 ing your creative abilities with a simple craft or art project. A great op
 portunity to socialize in a relaxed and friendly space. Materials provided
 \, but feel free to bring in something you're already working on!\nWed Nov
  25 - Christmas Crafts\nWed Dec 30 - Collage
LOCATION:College/Shaw\, Basement auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac94070ebad2200454442ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
